 ) 
Nh7+ 2. Kf5 Nf6 3. Be4 { In the following, there are many different move orders leading to the goal, but one thing to keep in mind is that White should push h4-h5 only when the king can't be expelled from g5, since in that case, Black would get access to the h6-square for their king, just as in the game. For this reason, the bishop will be well placed close to e6, since from that square, it could dominate a knight on h6. } Nh7 4. Bd3 ( 4. g4 { is also possible, now that Black can't sacrifice the knight on that pawn. } ) 
